    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d802">

                <pb facs="0926" n="914" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg914"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1930/27161: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-01-23T19:00:00-04:00">January 23, 1943—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>193. For Tittmann. Your 11, January 12.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d802-f1"/> A reply
                    along the lines suggested by you meets with the Department’s approval should you
                    be questioned concerning the possible bombardment of Rome. For your information
                    this subject has had the active attention of the President and ourselves. Mr.
                    Taylor has discussed the matter with the Apostolic Delegate who has undoubtedly
                    communicated these conversations to the Vatican.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
